Vendor/Vorssaint is Vorssaint's source as it is, built as a library. From 0.90.0 on Sonary runs
Vorssaint's features for everything: the system monitor, mouse, keyboard, Dynamic Island,
clipboard, apps, windows, display, sound, keep awake and tools. Sonary's own modules for these
stay in Packages/ and are meant to take over again one at a time. Changes made for Sonary, all of
them in that folder:
- `main.swift` left out and `Package.swift` rewritten, so the code builds as a library; the target is
  compiled without optimization, because Xcode's optimizer did not finish on it
- `Sources/Vorssaint/SonaryBridge.swift` added (Sonary's entry point; not Vorssaint's work)
- the name "Vorssaint" replaced by "Sonary" in the text shown to the user (`Core/*.swift`), as
  Vorssaint's trademark policy asks of forks; copyright lines are untouched
- `Services/Notch/NotchWindowHost.swift`: the island takes Sonary's accent colour
- `UI/Settings/SettingsCard.swift`: cards and rows drawn in the look of Sonary's own;
  `UI/Settings/GeneralSettings.swift`: `MenuBarGlyph` shows Sonary's menu bar icon
- `App/StatusItemController.swift`: shows readouts only, no icon of its own, and can tell its
  status bar windows from the host's
- calls that opened Vorssaint's settings window or closed its menu panel
  (`appDelegate()?.openSettingsWindow()`, `appDelegate()?.closePopover()`) now ask Sonary for its
  settings window and panel (`SonaryHost`), in 12 files under `UI/` and `Services/`

Sparkle (https://sparkle-project.org) is used as a dependency for in-app updates (MIT license).
